  "notes": "Units of each currency per one euro, as the ECB prints them (published around 16:00 CET on working days, the rate is for that day). One observation per currency, `key` is the ISO code; the file keeps the latest reference day only. ECB copyright conditions (read 2026-10-25): use is free if the information appears accurately, the ECB is cited, and any modification is stated. NIS per unit of another currency is a cross rate computed by the site (ILS per EUR divided by the currency per EUR). The ECB's rates are reference rates, not rates at which anyone trades; the Bank of Israel's representative rates stay a link (D20).",
